The fixtures of contract-test's workspace checks (workspaceChecks in
lean/ContractTest/Editor/Workspace.lean and workspaceFailures in
lean/ContractTest/Editor/Workspace/Contract.lean), which `mise run ffi-test` hands
contract-test as its second argument. It must stay executable (mode 100755).

- git: stands for git. It answers exactly the two command lines the
  workspace finder runs (lean/Editor/Workspace.lean): `rev-parse
  --path-format=absolute --show-toplevel --git-common-dir --abbrev-ref
  HEAD` prints the three lines of the file `fixture-git` in the nearest
  directory, the one it runs in or an ancestor, that holds one, and exits
  128 when none does; `remote get-url origin` prints the line of
  `fixture-origin` there, and exits 2 when there is none. Any other command
  line exits 2 with a message. Shell builtins only.
